2026-09-27T10:00:45.9309829Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9310222Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9310533Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9311255Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9312124Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9312217Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9312402Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9312675Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9312935Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9313021Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9313217Z ================
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9313335Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9313496Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9313839Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9314048Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9314159Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9314419Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9314577Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9314722Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9315096Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9315433Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9316590Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9317463Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9317637Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9318402Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9319305Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9319752Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9320314Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9321045Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9321195Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9321515Z ========
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9321706Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9323828Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9326396Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9326773Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9327534Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9328868Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9329527Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9400503Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9401285Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9402145Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9402351Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9402800Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9403041Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9404846Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9407174Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9408349Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9409890Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:00:45.9410263Z 
